 " of cyclic words."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d5573e4a-2c30-4caa-a029-7891b529b25b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bracket is the operation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cd9eef57-d7a5-4162-bd99-f23f5b534d8e"],
 " of the involutive bi-Lie structure. It gives, for two cyclic words, the \
sum over one particle of each of the pairing value of the two particles, \
times a Koszul sign, times the cyclic word made of the two remainders."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the bracket is the sum of ChordContraction \
over every pair of positions, and ChordContraction is exported because it is \
the one term the bracket and the co-bracket share and the published notebook \
shows the chord sum term by term. The function reads the degrees and the \
pairing values off the GradedPairing object and carries its own linearity \
rules, so a scalar multiple or a sum of products, the natural output of the \
products, composes without a wrapper. A product whose head disagrees with the \
convention of the pairing returns unevaluated rather than being coerced, \
since coercing would reinterpret a symmetric product as an exterior one and \
change signs. A single remaining factor is the word itself, never a \
one-factor product, the rule every product of the paclet follows. Alternative \
name considered: InvolutiveBracket, the name until 2026-09-30. Prior art: the \
Wolfram Language has no cyclic words or involutive bi-Lie structures; the \
engine the verification suites load computes the same bracket from letter \
strings and pins this function on every pair of words to total length 7.", 
       "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->763785024,ExpressionUUID->"cd668fe3-c028-45b8-ad34-f41f7287f2d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bracket is the sum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ChordContraction"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/ChordContraction",
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4458d139-cb8b-4063-b5ac-bd8ac6c52ce9"],
 " over every pair of positions."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fd69efa7-0c81-4913-b8b9-c081db4bd770"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " selects the picture: ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Symmetric\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "84401bae-435f-4eb2-ad5d-bb36af74091a"],
 " gives the bracket of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SymmetricProduct"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SymmetricProduct",
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1ada20cb-285c-43ab-b24f-3a9a5c930923"],
 " grading, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Exterior\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c2accc11-9255-47cb-9664-72f160f5afd8"],
 " that of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ExteriorProduct"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/ExteriorProduct", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "437a7b5d-06d0-4df5-a2ca-75a8096e7ac2"],
 " grading. The two differ by signs, not by the contraction."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"01533f27-73d1-4248-ae3e-5952b95b9288"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the two-argument form the bracket is applied to each pair of factors of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " in turn, with the Koszul sign of the shuffle, and the other factors are \
carried along. The extension lowers the number of factors by one, so it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1156e1de-7b17-466e-9625-7073cd3ada6d"],
 " on a single cyclic word, and a single remaining factor is the word \
itself."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1bb9343e-546a-495d-90bb-ddb1529aeef9"],

Cell["\<\
Both forms are linear: they distribute over sums and pull out scalars.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"623143b4-7130-45c8-8a37-d77796970c14"],

Cell["A word may be given as the list of its particles.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"65256c2a-2d78-4154-acc7-564884422e72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A product whose head disagrees with the convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " returns unevaluated."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"44c2e986-bf76-4dee-8c05-e16a60f5f914"],

